## 9. Buying guides

**Choosing by astrology.** Start from the birth chart. Use the Moon sign or ascendant ruler for a Navagraha attar, the janma nakshatra for a nakshatra attar, or the sun sign for a zodiac attar. See [Choose an Attar Based on Your Birth Chart]({{ base }}/blogs/news/choose-an-attar-based-on-your-birth-chart-birth-chart-fragrance-guide) and [Which Planet Controls Your Fragrance]({{ base }}/blogs/news/which-planet-controls-your-fragrance-discover-the-perfect-attar-according-to-vedic-astrology).

**Choosing by personality or occasion.** See [How to Choose the Right Attar for Your Personality]({{ base }}/blogs/news/blogs-attar-best-attar-for-your-personality-guide), [Fragrance and Personality]({{ base }}/blogs/news/fragrance-personality-what-your-favorite-scent-says-about-you) and [Best Attars for Office Wear]({{ base }}/blogs/news/blogs-attar-guide-best-attars-for-office-wear).

**Choosing by longevity.** See [Best Long Lasting Attars in India]({{ base }}/blogs/news/https-www-anandrasa-com-blog-best-long-lasting-attars-india) and [Top 10 Luxury Attars in India]({{ base }}/blogs/news/top-10-luxury-attars-in-india).

**Choosing incense.** See [The Complete Guide to Choosing the Right Agarbatti]({{ base }}/blogs/news/blogs-incense-agarbatti-buying-guide-mood-ritual) and [Natural vs Synthetic Agarbatti]({{ base }}/blogs/news/blogs-incense-agarbatti-natural-vs-chemical-difference).

**First-time buyer guidance.** The 6 ml size at {{ currency }} 599 is the standard entry point for trying a composition. Buyers unsure of a scent direction commonly begin with a bestseller or a build-your-own multipack rather than committing to a single 12 ml bottle.

