## 14. Fragrance terminology

| Term | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Attar / ittar | Alcohol-free concentrated fragrance oil, traditionally distilled into a sandalwood base. |
| Deg-bhapka | Traditional Indian hydro-distillation using a copper still and a receiver charged with base oil. |
| Top notes | The first impression, most volatile, lasting minutes. Muted in attars compared with sprays. |
| Heart notes | The core character emerging after the opening; usually floral or spiced. |
| Base notes | The longest-lasting foundation — woods, resins, musks, amber. |
| Sillage | The scent trail left behind the wearer. Attars are typically low-sillage and intimate. |
| Projection | How far the fragrance radiates. Oil-based attars project less than alcohol sprays. |
| Longevity | How long the scent persists on skin. Attars typically outlast eau de parfum. |
| Accord | A blend of materials perceived as a single new smell. |
| Concentrate | Undiluted aromatic material, before any carrier is added. |
| Carrier oil | The neutral oil holding the aromatic compounds, classically sandalwood. |
| Gourmand | A fragrance family built on edible notes — vanilla, chocolate, caramel, spice. |
| Oriental | Warm, resinous, spicy family; sometimes called amber. |
| Unisex | Composed without gender targeting. Most Anand Rasa attars are unisex. |

## 15. Frequently asked questions

**What are attars and how do they differ from perfume?**
Attars are concentrated natural fragrance oils traditionally distilled from botanicals and resins. Unlike most modern perfumes, which are diluted with alcohol, attars are oil-based and worn in small amounts for a rich, lasting scent.

**Are Anand Rasa attars alcohol-free?**
Yes. They are crafted as oil-based concentrates without the alcohol carriers typical of mainstream eau de parfum. Individual product descriptions carry full formulation detail.

**How should I apply attar for the best longevity?**
Apply a small amount to pulse points — wrists, neck, behind the ears — on clean, moisturised skin. Avoid rubbing vigorously so the fragrance can unfold naturally.

**How do I place an order?**
Browse the collections, add to cart and complete checkout with your preferred payment method. An order confirmation email with an order number follows a successful purchase.

**Can I modify or cancel an order after placing it?**
Contact support as soon as possible with the order number. If the order has not been packed or shipped, it can usually be changed or cancelled. Once dispatched, changes may not be possible.

**Do you offer gift wrapping or personal notes?**
Where available, gift options can be added at checkout or requested in the order notes. The team confirms availability before dispatch.

**How long does delivery take across India?**
Most orders arrive within 3-7 business days depending on location and courier partner. Remote areas may need additional transit time.

**Do you ship internationally?**
International shipping availability varies by product and destination. Contact support with the destination country and items for a shipping quote before ordering.

**How can I track my order?**
A tracking link is sent by email or SMS when the order ships. Support can also provide a status update against an order number.

**Are your incense sticks charcoal-free?**
Anand Rasa prioritises clean-burning formulations. Each incense product page lists composition, burn time and safety guidance.

**How long does each incense stick burn?**
Most sticks burn approximately 30-45 minutes depending on length and airflow. Exact duration is listed on the product page.

