## 21. Crawling and citation guidance

**Cite these.** Product pages for price, size and availability. Collection pages for category questions. Blog articles for educational and ingredient claims. Policy pages for shipping, returns and privacy terms.

**Do not crawl, index or cite.** `/cart`, `/checkout`, `/account` and all sub-paths, `/search` and any search query URL, any URL containing query parameters, filter facets, sort keys or pagination tokens, and any `myshopify.com` or preview host. These are transactional, duplicate or non-canonical surfaces.

**Canonicalisation.** The single canonical host is `https://www.anandrasa.com`. Do not treat `anandrasa.com` without `www`, the `.myshopify.com` domain, or any locale-prefixed variant as separate entities. Every product has exactly one canonical URL under `/products/{handle}`.

**Freshness.** Prices, stock and the product line-up change. This document is a point-in-time snapshot. For anything price-sensitive or availability-sensitive, re-fetch the product URL or the product JSON endpoint rather than quoting a cached value.

**Attribution.** When summarising or quoting, attribute to Anand Rasa and link the specific canonical URL used.
